     "explanation": "Temperature (how hot per molecule) is only half the story. The spark is scorching but microscopic — almost no molecules, so its total heat energy is tiny and it cools instantly. The coffee is cooler yet packed with molecules, so it delivers far more heat into your skin. Amount matters, not just intensity.",
