     "explanation": "Caloric was supposed to be a **finite, conserved fluid** trapped in the metal. If so, boring should squeeze out a limited supply and then stop producing heat. Instead the heat was inexhaustible — it kept coming as long as the drill turned, and a blunt drill (fewer chips) made even more heat. Something produced without limit cannot be a material substance, so heat had to be motion.",
