     "explanation": "This is the central distinction of the whole book. The First Law says the AMOUNT of energy never changes — even at heat death, all the energy is still there. The Second Law governs its QUALITY: as entropy maxes out, energy becomes perfectly uniform, with no hot-cold gradient to drive an engine. Extractable work requires a difference; a smoothed-out universe has none. Energy conserved, usefulness gone.",
